cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this pipeline or its outputs, please cite it as below."
title: "Rule vs. Exemplar Learning of Turkish Plural Allomorphy: dataset and nonce-item pipeline"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Erkiraz
    given-names: Buse
  - family-names: Mojoudi
    given-names: Niyousha
date-released: 2026-09-19
repository-code: "https://github.com/buseerkiraz/turkish-plural-allomorphy"
license: MIT
abstract: >
  A data-processing pipeline that classifies Turkish nominals for plural
  suffix allomorphy (-lar / -ler) from the TELL lexicon, isolates the Arabic
  -At exception neighbourhood, audits it for transcription circularity,
  codes a six-dimension binary feature matrix, and builds a screened
  nonce-word test set, produced for the course "From Neurons to
  Transformers: Cognitive Principles in AI Research" (Heidelberg University,
  SoSe 2026).
